EXPLAIN FORMAT=TREE SELECT DISTINCT tt1.a FROM t1 AS tt1 JOIN t1 AS tt2 ON tt1.a > tt2.a WHERE tt1.a + tt2.a IN (SELECT a FROM t1 AS tt3);
EXPLAIN
-> Table scan on <temporary>  (cost=X rows=X)
    -> Temporary table with deduplication  (cost=X rows=X)
        -> Nested loop inner join with distinct optimization  (cost=X rows=X)
            -> Nested loop inner join with distinct optimization  (cost=X rows=X)
                -> Table scan on tt1  (cost=X rows=X)
                -> Filter: (tt1.a > tt2.a)  (cost=X rows=X)
                    -> Table scan on tt2  (cost=X rows=X)
            -> Limit: 1 row(s)  (cost=X rows=X)
                -> Filter: ((tt1.a + tt2.a) = `<subquery2>`.a)  (cost=X rows=X)
                    -> Single-row index lookup on <subquery2> using <auto_distinct_key> (a=(tt1.a + tt2.a))  (cost=X rows=X)
                        -> Materialize with deduplication  (cost=X rows=X)
                            -> Filter: (tt3.a is not null)  (cost=X rows=X)
                                -> Table scan on tt3  (cost=X rows=X)

FLUSH STATUS;
